                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Fin
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi J
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Fin(J)
            is a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/directed+set"} directed set
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/filtered+category"} filtered category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Fin
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi J
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi op
                  %mo →
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Fin(J)^op\to C
            mapping the inclusion
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                  %mo ⊆
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F\subseteq G
            to
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi π
                    %mrow
                      %mi G
                      %mo ,
                      %mi F
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_{G,F}
            defined above is hence a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cofiltered+diagram"} cofiltered diagram
          %p
            We say that an object is an
            %strong
              infintary tensor product of the family
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mi i
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi J
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X_i)_{i\in J}
            in
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mi J
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_J
          %ul
            %li
              It is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cofiltered+limit"} cofiltered limit
              of the functor
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Fin
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi J
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi op
                    %mo →
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Fin(J)^op\to C
              described above, and moreover
            %li
              For every object
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo :
                    %mi C
                    %mo →
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A\otimes-:C\to C
              preserves this limit.
          %h2#examples Examples
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                In a
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cartesian+monoidal+category"} cartesian monoidal category
            %li
              %p
                More generally, consider a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cartesian+monoidal+category"} cartesian monoidal category
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝒞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
                and a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+monad"} monoidal monad
                (or
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutative+monad"} commutative monad
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi T
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+monad#monoidal_structure_on_the_kleisli_category"} the Kleisli category of a monoidal monad is canonically a monoidal category
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝒞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
                exists, and express it as a cofiltered limit of finite products. The
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+adjoint"} left adjoint
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝒞
                      %mo →
                      %msub
                        %mi 𝒞
                        %mi T
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}\to\mathcal{C}_T
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/preserved+limit"} preserves
                this limit if and only if the endofunctor
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi T
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
                does (see
                = succeed ")." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kleisli+category#Tlim"} here
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+monad"} monoidal monad
                on it which preserves
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cofiltered+limits"} cofiltered limits
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kleisli+category"} Kleisli category
                has infinitary tensor products.
            %li
              %p
                In a
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Markov+category"} Markov category
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Markov+category#kolmogorov_products"} Kolmogorov products
                are particular infinitary products compatible with the copy-discard structure. In particular, the category
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/BorelStoch"} BorelStoch
                has all countable infinitary tensor products.
            %li
              %p
                The
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Giry+monad"} Giry monad
                on
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/standard+Borel+spaces"} standard Borel spaces
                is an instance of both of the examples above, by the
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kolmogorov+extension+theorem"} Kolmogorov extension theorem
            %li
              %p
                Reversing all arrows, the
                %em infinite tensor product of rings
                is defined as the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/filtered+colimit"} filtered colimit
                of all the finitary tensor products. (The canonical arrows
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi I
                      %mo →
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I\to X
                are the units of the rings.)
